<title>SWITZERLAND: Memphis top world cargo airport in Mar 97 - ACI.</title>
<headline>Memphis top world cargo airport in Mar 97 - ACI.</headline>
<dateline>GENEVA 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Memphis, base of U.S. express freight carrier, Federal Express, was the world's busiest cargo airport in March 1997, said Geneva-based Airports Council International (ACI) in a survey of 495 airports worldwide.</p>
<p>The world's 20 busiest cargo airports in March 1997, with the volume in tonnes and percentage change from March 1996, were as follows:</p>
<p>    1 (1)  Memphis	     175,837   up    16.2 pct</p>
<p>    2 (2)  Los Angeles	 162,743   up    10.1</p>
<p>    3 (4)  Tokyo-Narita	157,476   up    10.0</p>
<p>    4 (7)  Hong Kong	   156,289   up    24.7</p>
<p>    5 (3)  Miami		 147,030   up     1.5</p>
<p>    6 (5)  New York/JFK	146,323   up     3.3</p>
<p>    7 (6)  Frankfurt	   139,843   up     4.9</p>
<p>    8 (8)  Seoul		 138,472   up    18.8</p>
<p>    9 (11) Singapore	   121,959   up    19.0</p>
<p>   10 (13) Chicago	     115,220   up    19.3</p>
<p>   11 (9)  Louisville	  112,845   down   2.4</p>
<p>   12 (10) Amsterdam	   110,922   up     6.3</p>
<p>   13 (14) Anchorage*	  110,726   up    24.6</p>
<p>   14 (12) London Heathrow   104,935   up     5.4</p>
<p>   15 (15) Paris CDG	    90,103   up     5.4</p>
<p>   16 (16) New York Newark    83,023   up     3.2</p>
<p>   17 (18) Taipei		 81,074   up    24.2</p>
<p>   18 (-)  Bangkok		70,458   up    17.8</p>
<p>   19 (17) Atlanta		68,567   up     1.8</p>
<p>   20 (19) Dallas Fort Worth  67,980   up     6.7</p>
<p>* includes freight and mail in transit as well as loaded/unloaded.</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Service Tel+ 44 171 542 7706 Fax +5017 - www.racs.com</p>
</text>
